"""Hard-questions lessons: an opening that sets the tone, a line to carry away and a check for understanding."""
R = {
'8-9-1': dict(hook='Ask: “Where did you first hear that you have to choose between faith and science?” Take a few answers, then say that the Church has never taught that.', mem='“The heavens declare the glory of God, and the firmament proclaims his handiwork.” (Psalm 19:1)', assess='Ask students to explain what Genesis 1 teaches and what questions science answers.'),
'8-9-2': dict(hook='Ask: “Is it harder to admit a family member’s mistake or your own?” Frame the lesson as honest history from people who love the Church.', mem='“Let both grow together until the harvest.” (Matthew 13:30)', assess='Ask students to describe one event from two points of view and say what the Church has acknowledged.'),
'8-9-3': dict(hook='Acknowledge that many students have faced pain. Invite quiet before beginning, and give permission to step out.', mem='“My grace is sufficient for you, for my power is made perfect in weakness.” (2 Corinthians 12:9)', assess='Ask students to state what the Church teaches about God and evil and one way to accompany someone who suffers.'),
'9-9-1': dict(hook='Say plainly that this lesson is about real harm and real accountability, and that anyone may step out. Follow your diocese’s safe-environment policy.', mem='“Whoever receives one such child in my name receives me.” (Matthew 18:5)', assess='Ask students to list what a safe community requires and where to report concerns.'),
'9-9-2': dict(hook='Ask: “Name women who shaped the Church.” List them before addressing the question of ordination.', mem='“Behold, I am the handmaid of the Lord.” (Luke 1:38)', assess='Ask students to explain the Church’s reasons for ordaining only men and name three roles women hold.'),
'9-9-3': dict(hook='Ask: “What would you give up for something you loved completely?” Introduce celibacy as a gift with a purpose.', mem='“There are eunuchs who have made themselves eunuchs for the sake of the kingdom of heaven. Let the one who is able to receive this receive it.” (Matthew 19:12)', assess='Ask students to explain why celibacy is a discipline and where Eastern Catholic priests differ.'),
'10-9-1': dict(hook='Say that some students in the room may have lived through this, and that the aim is truth with compassion. Anyone may step out.', mem='“Before I formed you in the womb I knew you.” (Jeremiah 1:5)', assess='Ask students to state the Church’s teaching and name three ways to support women and families in crisis.'),
'10-9-2': dict(hook='Acknowledge that many Catholics have never heard this teaching, and that the aim is to understand it, not to shame anyone.', mem='“Be fruitful and multiply.” (Genesis 1:28)', assess='Ask students to explain the Church’s teaching in their own words and describe how NFP differs from contraception.'),
'10-9-3': dict(hook='Ask: “Is chastity about saying no, or about saying yes to something?” Take answers.', mem='“Do you not know that your body is a temple of the Holy Spirit?” (1 Corinthians 6:19)', assess='Ask students to define chastity and write a personal rule for friendships and screens.'),
'11-9-1': dict(hook='Acknowledge that divorce touches many families in the room and that this lesson is not about blaming anyone.', mem='“What therefore God has joined together, let not man put asunder.” (Mark 10:9)', assess='Ask students to explain the difference between divorce and annulment and what the tribunal examines.'),
'11-9-2': dict(hook='Set ground rules: listen, no jokes, no personal questions. Let students step out. Open with the Church’s call to respect every person.', mem='“Love one another as I have loved you.” (John 13:34)', assess='Ask students to state the Church’s teaching and describe how to treat a friend with love and truth.'),
'11-9-3': dict(hook='Acknowledge that some students have lost someone. Open with a moment of silence for those who have died.', mem='“Even though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death, I fear no evil, for you are with me.” (Psalm 23:4)', assess='Ask students to distinguish euthanasia from refusing burdensome treatment and describe good palliative care.'),
'12-10-1': dict(hook='Ask: “When is it right to use force? When is it never right?” List answers before the criteria.', mem='“Blessed are the peacemakers.” (Matthew 5:9)', assess='Ask students to state why the Church calls the death penalty inadmissible and apply the just war criteria to a case.'),
'12-10-2': dict(hook='Acknowledge that infertility is a deep suffering for many couples. Begin with compassion.', mem='“Children are a heritage from the Lord, the fruit of the womb a reward.” (Psalm 127:3)', assess='Ask students to explain why the Church distinguishes treatment from replacement of the marital act and name ethical options.'),
'12-10-3': dict(hook='Ask: “What do you think Catholics believe happens to people of other faiths?” Collect answers before reading the Catechism.', mem='“I am the way, and the truth, and the life. No one comes to the Father except through me.” (John 14:6)', assess='Ask students to explain what the Church teaches about salvation outside the visible Church.'),
}
